hello i'm greg sadler the editor of  stoicism today a member of the modern  stoicism team and one of the organizers  this year for  stoicon the world's largest annual  gathering of people interested in  stoicism both in its ancient and modern  forms and i want to tell you all about  it first of all i want to give you a  save the date so it's coming up a little  under two months from my talking to you  right now on october  9th that's a saturday and it's going to  be an online event again this year so  you don't have to travel to get to it  you can mark it on your calendar and you  don't have to worry about jostling with  anybody else to get into a packed room  we are going to have enough room for as  many attendees as want to show up last  year it was over a thousand people who  were there for the event virtually and  we'll probably have even more this time  so once again on saturday october 9th  put it on your calendar we are going to  have an eventbrite  event page that will allow you to sign  up for it and and purchase a ticket  purchasing means actually just making a  donation this year just as last year  we'll also be having an announcement  post shortly in stoicism today the  official blog of the modern stoicism  organization that is putting on stoicon  and we're going to have a lot of other  stuff coming up in stoicism today  including interviews with some of the  speakers and other announcements about  cool things related to stoicon and stoic  week so stay tuned  for all of that all those follow-ups i  would like to mention  my other  fellow organizers and co-organizers so  andy shaka and i  have taken on the task of the main  organization we are ably assisted by  phil yanov and harold kavli and a whole  host of other people that will be  working behind the scenes to provide a  really great and engaging experience for  you and an opportunity to not only learn  about stoicism but connect with other  people that are interested in that  tickets will be available on the  eventbrite site as i mentioned it's  donations so you know you give what you  think you  ought to give or what you would like to  give and everybody has different income  levels  so you don't have to feel bad if you if  you can't give anything we're still  happy to have you there if you want to  give a big donation that's great too all  of the proceeds will be going to the  modern stoicism organization a  non-profit that puts on stoicons  supports stoic on x's provides stoic  week provides a whole bunch of other  online seminars and classes all  dedicated to  helping people learn about and apply  ancient philosophy  in their modern lives so on the day of  the event there will be a zoom link that  gets sent to everybody who has tickets  so you don't have to ask about that  ahead of time that'll all be made  available  at the at the right time i do want to  give a short bit of history before  telling you about how the event is set  up this year  so  we're almost approaching a decade of  stoicons which is a really cool thing to  be able to say it started out in london  with a you know a kind of informal but  still structured meeting of philosophers  psychotherapists a few other people that  actually got some attention and it was  connected with live like a stoic week  and then it grew and became  something that we identify as  stoicon the world's largest gathering of  stoics and people interested in stoics  in history and it grew every year at  first it was taking place in london then  it went across the atlantic to new york  then it was in toronto back to london  again then to athens greece and then of  course  coronavirus hit and we had to go online  and we had an even bigger event last  year in 2020  entirely virtual so we decided to do  that again this year because not only  you know can we not predict what's going  to happen with the coronavirus but it  offered the opportunity  to engage people  worldwide in a way that the main  physical face-to-face conference  although it was great  wasn't actually able to do so we're  really happy to have anybody who wants  to come and participate we have a lot of  great speakers  lined up um we're making it even more  interactive this year we've been putting  a lot of thought and planning  into that we've got five talks which  will be anywhere from you know 20 15 to  20 minutes each with some q a  afterwards we've got speakers talking  about a whole variety of different  subjects so that's kind of the  traditional thing we also have a great  keynote coming up with nancy sherman so  that's something that i'm really looking  forward to but we have two  panels and ask the expert panel where  you get to contribute the questions all  be moderating and our experts  will be answering the questions for you  some of them will be provided ahead of  time by people and some of them will  take from the audience right there and  then  we're also going to have another panel  about applying stoicism with experts in  those sorts of fields ranging from  parenting to mindfulness to all sorts of  things in between  we're going to have a workshop led by  tim labon  which will have him providing us with  some guidance and content and then we'll  go into breakout rooms and we'll do work  together there and then come back as a  community and  share our results with each other and  we're also going to have lightning talks  this is a very popular feature that we  did in the past this year they will be  pre-recorded harold covley will be  emceeing that and and overseeing it and  that is a big treat as well it's a way  in which many people can get to speak  for a short amount of time these are  lightning talks you know three to five  minutes at a time those are a lot of fun  as well so we have all of that lined up  speakers are going to be coming and  zooming in from three different  continents it's going to be an all-day  affair the speakers include academics  therapists popular writers coaches  journalists many of them are members of  the modern stoicism team including some  recent additions but we have a whole  bunch of other people as well you'll be  able to go to the eventbrite page i'll  also put a you know sort of a  description of the different talks and  panels and things like that with the  speakers names in the video description  so you can go there as well and look for  the post coming out uh in stoicism today  and updates about stoicon as well and  don't forget stoicon comes before stoic  week another main event put on by modern  stoicism that you can participate in  we're going to be revamping it again  this year so lots of cool opportunities  for you to learn practice and engage  with others about stoicism  you
 

